{"_data": [{"contents": [{"type": "lesson_name", "content": ""}, {"type": "unit_name", "content": "Organizations and Information Systems"}, {"type": "position", "content": 9}, {"type": "origin", "content": "stub"}, {"type": "lesson", "content": 2}, {"type": "level", "content": "A2.2"}], "type": "metadata"}, {"contents": [{"type": "test", "content": "false"}], "type": "achievment_test"}, {"contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "These are words you hear/use when you talk about organizations and IT."}], "type": "target_word_describer"}, {"contents": [{"type": "primary", "content": "Identify key information about people's jobs and places of work in spoken or written contexts.  Build the IT system prototype, starting from the analysis of the functional characteristics of the system regarding user-friendliness, functionality and user experience, supported in software applied following design protocols."}, {"type": "secondary_1", "content": "Understands important information and aspects of attitude and intention in spoken situations in English on a range of common communicative topics related to this level. Exchanges simple information on the design of an information system, computer architecture and hardware, and basic concepts on graphic design."}], "type": "objectives"}, {"type": "background_image", "content": "enpe8n4le02ob09re1img01.jpg"}, {"contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": "Possessive Adjectives vs. Possessive Pronouns"}, {"type": "describer", "content": "You use possessives to talk about an object that belongs to you or other people."}, {"type": "example", "content": "Information systems need to ensure that their information isn't mixed with ours, or the clients', for example."}, {"type": "example", "content": "Imagine, my ideas can be preserved as well as yours, and then be shared with the entire team!"}, {"type": "text", "content": "We use possessive adjectives to talk about something that belongs to someone. As they are adjectives, you must use them before the object.<br><br>  Examples:<br> <span class= \"italic\">  <span class= \"strong\">My</span>  organization can benefit from your guidance.<br> <span class= \"strong\">Our</span>  team of managers were in charge of sales strategies.</span>  <br><br>  You use possessive pronouns when you have already mentioned the object that is owned, and you don't need to repeat it. As you already know, pronouns replace nouns to avoid unnecessary repetitions.<br><br>  Examples: <br> <span class= \"italic\">  Your firm has progressed just as much as <span class= \"strong\">ours</span> .<br> Her business influence is far stronger than <span class= \"strong\">mine</span> .</span> <br><br>  As you could see in the examples above, <span class= \"strong\">possessive adjectives</span>  have a different position within sentences when compared to <span class= \"strong\">possessive pronouns</span> . Possessive adjectives go right before the noun they are modifying, but <span class= \"strong\">possessive pronouns</span>  can go either at the end of the sentence or at the beginning when answering a question, for example.<br> <span class= \"italic\">  These are <span class= \"strong\">my</span>  books.<br> These books are <span class= \"strong\">mine</span> .<br>  - Are these your books?<br> - No,<span class= \"strong\"> mine</span>  are these ones. <br><br>  Remember that none of these words have apostrophes. <br><br>  In the chart below, you will find both types of possessives:"}, {"type": "table", "content": "{\"rows\":8,\"columns\":3,\"cells\":[\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"strong\\\"> Personal pronoun</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"strong\\\"> Possessive adjective</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"strong\\\"> Possessive pronoun</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"I\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"My\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Mine\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"You\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Your\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Yours\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"He\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"His\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"His\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"She\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Her\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Hers\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"It\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Its\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Its\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"We\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Our\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Ours\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"They\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Their\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Theirs\\\"}\"],\"styles\":\" instruction_table_background intro_table_border\"}"}], "type": "learning_points"}, {"contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": " Types of Organizations in Business"}, {"type": "describer", "content": "In order to determine what kind of organization is more convenient for you or your business partners, it is essential that you review the different options you have, as well as their pros and cons."}, {"type": "example", "content": "Speaking of organization types, there are three main types: sole proprietorship, partnership and corporations. The kind of organization we chose will influence the load of information our IT team will have to deal with."}, {"type": "text", "content": "<div align=\u201djustify\u201d>Here you will find some of the most common types of business organizations, including their characteristics and some of the advantages and disadvantages.</div><br><br>  <div class=\"center_text\"><span class= \"strong\">Sole Proprietorship</span> </div><br> <div align=\u201djustify\u201d>It is usually established by one individual. It offers great flexibility, low cost management, and it is easy to dissolve. However, all responsibility lies in the owner, since this person represents the entire business. Additionally, it's harder to find funding.</div><br><br>  <div class=\"center_text\"><span class= \"strong\">Partnership</span> </div><br> <div align=\u201djustify\u201d>When two or more people decide to do business, it offers the possibility of creating a business and sharing responsibilities. It's easier to find business capital, and less taxes than corporations. However, there may be problems among partners and that could lead to conflicts or withdrawals. Also, liabilities are very strong.</div><br><br>  <div class=\"center_text\"><span class= \"strong\">Corporation</span> </div><br> <div align=\u201djustify\u201d>They're the most common kind of organization in the US. They have unlimited business life because partners can't dissolve it easily. Ownership can be transferred by selling stock and liability is limited to stock prices and not personal profit. On the other hand, they are closely monitored by the government, they also pay higher taxes and operational costs.</div>"}], "type": "learning_points"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "sole"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "the only one, unique"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(adjective)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: If we select a simple type, like a sole proprietorship, the volume of information won't be too high."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "enpe8n4le02ob09aud01"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "partnership"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "when two or more business partners create an organization"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: However, with a partnership, we could have more managers, and each of them could have their own system profile containing their business deals, records and so on. "}, {"type": "audio", "content": "enpe8n4le02ob09aud02"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "business deal"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "an agreement or business transaction"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: However, with a partnership, we could have more managers, and each of them could have their own system profile containing their business deals, records and so on."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "enpe8n4le02ob09aud03"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "entire"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "whole, full or complete"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(adjective)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: Imagine, my ideas can be preserved as well as yours, and then be shared with the entire team!"}, {"type": "audio", "content": "enpe8n4le02ob09aud04"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "passionate"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "devoted to or enthusiastic about something"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(adjective)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: We need people who are passionate about technology, have expertise in this field, can solve problems easily and can work in teams!"}, {"type": "audio", "content": "enpe8n4le02ob09aud05"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "expertise"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "the amount of experience or skill in a field"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: we need people who are passionate about technology, have expertise in this field, can solve problems easily and can work in teams! "}, {"type": "audio", "content": "enpe8n4le02ob09aud06"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "Look for information about information systems."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Describe the different systems you find."}, {"type": "text", "content": "List the ones you can use in a corporation and their uses applying everything you learned in this lesson."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Share your findings with a partner."}], "type": "takeaway_extension"}, {"contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "I find information about information systems."}, {"type": "text", "content": "I describe information systems."}, {"type": "text", "content": "I list information systems I can use."}, {"type": "text", "content": "I share my findings with a partner"}], "type": "takeaway_assessment"}], "type": "sena", "labs": [{"exercises": [{"stimuli_ids": [0], "_data": [{"contents": [{"type": "Learning Outcomes", "content": "I can explain the relation between information systems and organizations."}, {"type": "Learning Outcomes", "content": "I can give detailed information related to Info systems and organizations."}, {"type": "Learning Outcomes", "content": "I can talk about the interaction between IT and organizations."}, {"type": "Free Header Item", "content": "What do you know about organizations and information technology? How are they related?"}, {"type": "Free Header Item", "content": "Does the size of the company, as well as its type, influence information load? Explain. "}], "type": "instructions"}, {"contents": [{"type": "group_name", "content": "Welcome"}], "type": "group"}, {"type": "feedback", "content": {"attempt_feedback": [{"type": "text", "content": "You have 2 tries"}, {"type": "text", "content": "you have 1 attempt left"}], "correct_feedback": "Correct", "incorrect_feedback": [{"type": "text", "content": "try again"}, {"type": "text", "content": "Maybe next time"}], "allowed_attempts": 2}}, {"type": "free_header_text", "content": "Ask y